2026-09-27T04:48:15.7509696Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7510070Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7510579Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7511114Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7511278Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7511628Z ================
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7511845Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7512066Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7512666Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7513040Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7513246Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7513730Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7514046Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7514296Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7514958Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7515566Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7516696Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7517934Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7518129Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7518923Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7519904Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7520414Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7520952Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7521646Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7521892Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7528206Z ========
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7528606Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7531059Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7533452Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7533828Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7534656Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7535458Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7536537Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7537744Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7538507Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7538979Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7539537Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7540134Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7643512Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7645600Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7647453Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7648135Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7649029Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:48:15.7649256Z 
